Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:29:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/45] Fix neurabash tool: match current OutputAccumulator API
 and error convention

npm run check caught two real issues after rebasing onto the 284-commit
upstream update:
- OutputAccumulator.snapshot()/closeTempFile() no longer take options
  (the persistIfTruncated param was removed upstream); the code here
  was still calling the old signature.
- AgentToolResult requires `details` when returned directly; switched
  the "binary not found" early-exit to throw, matching how every other
  tool in this codebase (bash.ts included) signals a pre-execution
  failure, instead of hand-rolling an isError object.

Also dropped an unused `cwd` parameter flagged by biome.

npm run check now passes clean: biome, tsgo --noEmit, installer,
push-guard, and browser-smoke all green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
